#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:5
#: f2cf7967925e4c6391f472dfc0f4682a
msgid "Tuning Navigation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:7
#: f19c9ee0113e41e89d362dcf71eb5cce
msgid "This page describes how to tune the Navigation control including \"S-Curves\" and the \"Position controller\".  The lower level :ref:`speed<rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed>` and :ref:`turn rate<rover-tuning-steering-rate>` controllers should be tuned before attempting to tune this controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:12
#: 739404c051d7476f98f8f15dfb016bc2
msgid "S-Curves and the position controller are used all the autonomous modes including :ref:`Auto<auto-mode>`, :ref:`Guided<guided-mode>`, :ref:`RTL<rtl-mode>` and :ref:`SmartRTL<smartrtl-mode>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:15
#: 6cc83c983812436dbe43980e8472dac6
msgid "S-Curves"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:17
#: fc88236774c74556830b438e4255b2dc
msgid "S-Curves are used to plan a smooth path that brings the vehicle close to each waypoint while not exceeding speed or acceleration limits.  The resulting path includes continuous position and 2D velocity targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:19
#: ad85176234214fe199166d05d5b865cf
msgid "Factors affecting the path include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:21
#: faf5bec79c8e47d3ab117abff9b75cce
msgid "The vehicle will cut the corners but will always try to pass within :ref:`WP_RADIUS<WP_RADIUS>` or :ref:`TURN_RADIUS<TURN_RADIUS>` (whichever is larger) of each waypoint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:22
#: a703396ed51649f891987e4fdf81e51d
msgid "The vehicle will cut the corners more at higher speeds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:23
#: feaf57b9bb5848ca869767aaed52fb82
msgid "The vehicle will cut the corners more if the maximum accelerations are reduced (e.g. the lowest of :ref:`ATC_ACCEL_MAX<ATC_ACCEL_MAX>`, :ref:`ATC_DECEL_MAX<ATC_DECEL_MAX>` and :ref:`ATC_TURN_MAX_G<ATC_TURN_MAX_G>` * 9.81)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:24
#: 352f0088bd644c5fa8a0ee180ba9c95f
msgid "The vehicle will slow down in the corners if necessary to pass within :ref:`WP_RADIUS<WP_RADIUS>` of the waypoint without exceeding the maximum accelerations (e.g. the lowest of :ref:`ATC_ACCEL_MAX<ATC_ACCEL_MAX>`, :ref:`ATC_DECEL_MAX<ATC_DECEL_MAX>` and :ref:`ATC_TURN_MAX_G<ATC_TURN_MAX_G>` * 9.81)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:25
#: 584507b5279f406b80c7f86f361cb2d8
msgid "Placing waypoints close together may lead to the vehicle traveling slowly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:28
#: 5cdc40fb8913458cbe5e413a076b1732
msgid "Position Controller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:30
#: b3f13d20886341a6a817aecdf9481033
msgid "The position controller is responsible for calculating the desired speed and turn rate so the vehicle follows the path between waypoints created by the S-Curves (see above).  The desired speed and turn rate are then passed to the lower level controllers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:32
#: 5d3b06dd612d40418bf53f062476c2a8
msgid "Method for tuning the position controller:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:34
#: 8871fbf16fbc4edf9f3c8113947e2e2f
msgid "Connect the ground station to the vehicle using a telemetry radio"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:35
#: 3345a52bae364c52be8eb8394a867edb
msgid "Create a rectangular or back-and-forth mission with long straight segments and upload to the vehicle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:40
#: c5a2a188651d41119510870102472438
msgid "Arm the vehicle (in :ref:`Manual<manual-mode>` or :ref:`Hold<hold-mode>`) and then switch to :ref:`Auto<auto-mode>` mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:41
#: d951c0c7453648d48797958049cb2e51
msgid "Adjust these parameters to improve the vehicle's tracking along the lines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:43
#: 25f38b4ff37f4b02afd54ec7cdd512eb
msgid "set :ref:`PSC_VEL_I<PSC_VEL_I>` and :ref:`PSC_VEL_D<PSC_VEL_D>` to zero"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:44
#: ddc3b66665a5441b95435c8902909eb2
msgid "increase :ref:`PSC_VEL_P<PSC_VEL_P>` until the vehicle tracks the corners nicely without oscillating in the straights"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:45
#: e0e6e944f3f7497e8e10bb20334875ab
msgid "increase :ref:`PSC_VEL_D<PSC_VEL_D>` enough to make the corners more responsive but without introducing oscillations in the straights.  This should normally be not more than 10% of :ref:`PSC_VEL_P<PSC_VEL_P>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:46
#: 425949a75a774d558ce0c4950218d65b
msgid "set :ref:`PSC_VEL_I<PSC_VEL_I>` to 20% of :ref:`PSC_VEL_P<PSC_VEL_P>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:48
#: 62857edb3a6f4c949037a6679f7d2a34
msgid "These values normally do not need to be changed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:50
#: 66dfda3e7c254c0292f9f6169ce4d554
msgid ":ref:`PSC_POS_P<PSC_POS_P>` should be left at 0.2 (the default).  This converts the position error into a desired velocity.  Higher values will lead to the vehicle trying to drive back to the line more quickly but if raised too high may lead to oscillation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:51
#: 7ead6e5d4c294b419d3e61fa4fbd0e0a
msgid ":ref:`PSC_VEL_FF<PSC_VEL_FF>` should always be 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:52
#: e6a6a8d7f060419ba112ccf514968a55
msgid ":ref:`PSC_VEL_IMAX<PSC_VEL_IMAX>` should always be 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:53
#: 5f43881849dd4b279ca2c6a52944a94f
msgid ":ref:`PSC_VEL_FLTD<PSC_VEL_FLTD>`, :ref:`PSC_VEL_FLTE<PSC_VEL_FLTE>` should be left at the default of 5 although small vehicle may benefit from higher values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:55
#: 7e78407d2cb0457c91abf2038779a010
msgid "It may also help to monitor the velocity controller PIDs in real-time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:57
#: 1e4cb25e753446d9aabb6121775e1db5
msgid "Ensure the mission has long straight segments aligned either North-South or West-East"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:62
#: 5a936343116844809ad2ba6cc91d2b1b
msgid "Enable real time PID reporting of the position controller's velocity controller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:64
#: ac9e5d9e7bd44a2fb46a28cecdfd78fa
msgid "If the mission runs West-East set GCS_PID_MASK = 64 (Velocity North)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:65
#: e36d217948d64dae9da4330b9e786290
msgid "If the mission runs North-South set GCS_PID_MASK = 128 (Velocity East)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:67
#: 3a18c09b06384addaa0a27a598fa7bdb
msgid "Display the real-time PID values on the ground station.  If using MP, go to the Data screen, check the \"Tuning\" checkbox.  Double click on the display area and select, \"piddesired\", \"pidachieved\", \"pidP\", \"pidI\" and \"pidD\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:73
#: 626e0879e03c4c28a0f80a132b4243c2
msgid "Other Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:75
#: d05255f044704b6bb9353e5736565757
msgid ":ref:`WP_SPEED<WP_SPEED>` defines the target speed (in m/s) that the vehicle will drive at in :ref:`Auto<auto-mode>` and :ref:`Guided<guided-mode>`.  It will also be used in :ref:`RTL<rtl-mode>` and :ref:`SmartRTL<smartrtl-mode>` if :ref:`RTL_SPEED<RTL_SPEED>` is set to zero"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:76
#: a4d90859fb9f4ca9b90384e0b04641f0
msgid ":ref:`WP_RADIUS<WP_RADIUS>` specifies the distance before the waypoint that the vehicle may begin turning towards the next waypoint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:79
#: 0041196f789d482c841bb3e0a077b6df
msgid "How the Position Controller works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:81
#: 819b966c7a464a1b8282c8bc62d5094a
msgid "Compares the vehicle's current location to the desired location and calculating a desired 2D velocity to close the gap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:82
#: 4636d2a881984c9b97bd230538007f49
msgid "Compares the vehicle's current velocity to the above velocity (aka position correction velocity) + the S-Curve provided velocity and calculating a desired 2D acceleration to reduce the error"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:83
#: 771b122421bf4bdab7e9b7a365ad9b91
msgid "The vehicle forward-back portion of position correction velocity + S-Curve velocity is the target forward speed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation.rst:84
#: 7046673b7f834253b2c7cdf06ee4a4e0
msgid "the lateral component of the 2D acceleration becomes the target turn rate"
msgstr ""
